    "updated_at": "2020-06-12T03:12:12Z",
    "body": "Version dependency shows up on Linux as well: with this config, mode-switching works in 3.0.2 and is broken in 3.1.0.\r\n\r\nBisecting [the fish repo](https://github.com/fish-shell/fish-shell) points to 8ff866b26b2f42bb8deeb2c2ec2b308c79daff75 being the first bad commit.\r\n\r\nCommit message:\r\n\r\n>     Add repaint-mode bind function\r\n>     \r\n>     If we switch the bind mode, we add a \"force-repaint\" there just to\r\n>     redraw the mode indicator.\r\n>     \r\n>     That's quite wasteful and annoying, considering that sometimes the prompt can take\r\n>     half a second.\r\n>     \r\n>     So we add a \"repaint-mode\" function that just reexecutes the\r\n>     mode-prompt and uses the cached values for the others.\r\n\r\nSeems relevant, though I don't understand the interaction between fish's various prompt functions well enough to explain why this only occurs under certain situations.",
