    "created_at": "2020-06-14T06:00:28Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-06-14T06:00:28Z",
    "body": "> I'm sorry, I'm not terribly familiar with all the bits of fish. What do you mean by fish_mode_prompt being bad?\r\n\r\nWhen `starship init fish` is run, it does this:\r\n```\r\nfunction fish_mode_prompt; end\r\n```\r\n\r\nAs long as I don't change the definition of `fish_mode_prompt` then starship updates the prompt with the vi mode properly. If I change `fish_mode_prompt` to be not empty then starship stops updating the vi mode. How does starship know to do this? Or is fish somehow doing it?\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
