    "created_at": "2020-06-15T23:35:03Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-06-15T23:35:19Z",
    "body": "I think this is being done by fish, as a feature in their newer versions.\r\n\r\nThe resolution to [fish-shell/#5783](https://github.com/fish-shell/fish-shell/issues/5783) added a new feature that skips executing `fish_prompt` if `fish_mode_prompt` is a non-empty function (or at least, that's how I'm reading it). The relevant commit is [here](https://github.com/fish-shell/fish-shell/commit/8ff866b26b2f42bb8deeb2c2ec2b308c79daff75), which appears to switch a bunch of `force-repaint` calls into `repaint-mode` calls.\r\n\r\nThis makes it faster to run expensive prompts without needing to redraw the entire prompt on mode-switch. Unfortunately, it breaks use cases where `fish_mode_prompt` is being used to trigger a redraw as a side effect (like here). I'm not sure if there's an easy way for us to switch it back.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
